    "contentEn": "Study the sources and answer the questions.\n\nSource A (district survey, 1 200 respondents aged 15–24)\n- Intend to work or start a business in a mainland Greater Bay Area city within five years: 31%\n- Have not considered it: 44%\n- Would not consider it: 25%\n- Among those intending to go, the reasons most often cited were \"more development opportunities\" (62%) and \"lower cost of living\" (48%)\n\nSource B (a young respondent)\n\"It is not that I do not want to go. I do not know how I would come back. Recognition of professional qualifications, social security, schooling for children — these are not questions a single talk can answer.\"\n\n(a) Using Source A, describe young people’s attitudes to working across the boundary, and identify one thing the survey does not show.\n(b) What kind of barrier do the concerns in Source B represent? Use figures from Source A to show how the two relate.\n(c) As a policymaker, propose two measures that would lower this kind of barrier, explaining what each specifically targets.",
    "explanationEn": "The second half of (a) is a standing requirement in data-response work: say what the source does not show. A good answer does not simply call the data insufficient but names the missing item that would change the reading — the background distribution of the sample, for instance, since if respondents cluster in one group the 31% cannot represent young people generally.\nPart (b) is the crux: the individual statement in Source B must be linked back to the figures in Source A, and the link is the difference between \"have not considered\" and \"would not consider\". The two sound similar in ordinary speech but differ entirely in policy terms — one is unevaluated, the other evaluated and refused. Making that point answers the relation the question asks for.\nThe measures in (c) must address institutional barriers. Proposing more publicity or more exchange tours is the commonest loss, because Source B states outright that these are not questions a single talk can answer — the question has already excluded that class of answer.",
    "markingScheme": "（a）3 分 —— 準確描述三個比例並指出「未有考慮」為最大一群（1）；引用有意北上者的兩項理由並作出詮釋（1）；具體指出一項調查未能顯示的資訊（1）。答「資料不足」而無具體所指不給分。\n（b）4 分 —— 正確辨認為制度性障礙（1）；舉出資料二中至少兩項具體事例（1）；引用 44% 這個數字（1）；說明「未有考慮」與「不會考慮」的分別，並連回資料二所指的不確定性（1）。\n（c）3 分 —— 兩項措施各 1 分，須針對制度層面；另 1 分予針對性的說明是否確實回應資料二所提出的顧慮。純宣傳或交流活動類措施不給分。\n本題所列分數為本平台練習用尺度，並非香港考試及評核局的分數分配。參考答案只列必達步驟與判準，刻意不提供可直接抄錄的完整答卷。交卷後請逐項對照自評，機器不會為本題評分。",
